yes(808,'C','At 298.15 K, standard molar gas entropies are approximately HF 173.8, HCl 186.9, HBr 198.7 and HI 206.6 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹. HI has the largest value in this series.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry/pages/g-standard-thermodynamic-properties-for-selected-substances'],question='Which hydrogen halide has the highest standard molar entropy as a gas at 298.15 K?',options=['HBr','HF','HI','HCl'],audit='Specified standard gaseous comparison; verified all four primary table entries, not mass trend alone.',check='entropy-ranking')
yes(809,'A','For Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag, one mole of electrons deposits one mole of silver. Q = It = 10 × 4830 = 48,300 C. Mass = 48,300/96,500 × 108 = 54.055 g, or 54.1 g to one decimal place.',[EL],question='What mass of silver is deposited by a 10 A current through an Ag⁺ solution for 4830 s, at 100% current efficiency? [Ag = 108 g mol⁻¹; F = 96,500 C mol⁻¹]',options=['54.1 g','27.0 g','13.5 g','108.0 g'],audit='Source A54.0 updated54.1 for supplied4830s/F96500; retained all numerical inputs and explained correct rounding.',check='silver-faraday')
no(810,'SO2 acts as both agents, but H2 does too: oxidised toH+ with nonmetals and reduced toH− in metal hydrides. Broad stem has multiple valid answers; no specified reaction context.')
yes(811,'B','H₂ + I₂ ⇌ 2HI has two moles of gas on each side. Compression at fixed temperature scales numerator and denominator of its pressure quotient equally, so it causes no equilibrium shift in the ideal-gas approximation.',[REB],question='Which ideal-gas equilibrium does not shift when volume decreases at fixed temperature?',options=['2O₃(g) ⇌ 3O₂(g)','H₂(g) + I₂(g) ⇌ 2HI(g)','2NO₂(g) ⇌ N₂O₄(g)','PCl₅(g) ⇌ PCl₃(g) + Cl₂(g)'],audit='Restored all gas states/equilibrium arrows; removed following CO question from D.',check='equal-gas-moles')
